<title>USA: Ky. Commission $200 mln notes repriced, yield cut.</title>
<headline>Ky. Commission $200 mln notes repriced, yield cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. said Tuesday it repriced Kentucky Asset/Liability Commission's $200 million note deal, cutting the yield to 3.85 percent from 3.90 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows: </p>
<p>KENTUCKY ASSET/LIABILITY COMMISSION</p>
<p>RE: $200,400,000*</p>
<p>GENERAL FUND TAX AND REVENUE ANTICIPATION NOTES</p>
<p>SERIES 1997 A</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p> MOODY'S: MIG-1	     S&amp;P: SP-1+		 FITCH: F-1+</p>
<p> DATED: 07/10/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 06/25/1998</p>
<p>DUE: 06/25</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>06/25/1998	    200,400M    4.500 %	  3.85</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 100.600)</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Wednesday, July 9, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on July 10, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. Inc.</p>
<p>J.J.B. Hilliard, W.L. Lyons, Inc.</p>
<p>J.C. Bradford &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Morgan Keegan &amp; Co., Inc.</p>
<p>First Kentucky Securities Corp.</p>
<p>Ross Sinclaire &amp; Associates Inc.</p>
<p>Seasongood &amp; Mayer</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
